     "options": [],
     "answer": "The inner lining of the stomach secretes: 1. Mucus: Protects the stomach wall from its own acid. 2. Hydrochloric Acid (HCl): Kills ingested pathogens and creates an acidic medium (pH 1.5–2.5). 3. Digestive Gastric Juices (Pepsin): Breaks down complex dietary proteins into simpler peptides.",
