     "marks": 2,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Why birds do not need teeth?",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "Birds do not possess teeth because teeth and heavy jaw bones would add excessive weight, impeding flight. Instead, birds swallow food whole into the crop for softening, after which a muscular, pebble-filled organ called the Gizzard grinds the food mechanically with tremendous force.",
