     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Why are the handles of cooking utensils made of wood or plastic, while their bodies are made of metal?",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "Metals (aluminium, stainless steel, copper) are excellent thermal conductors that transfer flame heat quickly and evenly to cook the food. Conversely, wood and Bakelite plastic are thermal insulators (poor conductors); their handles remain cool to touch, protecting the cook from severe burns.",
