     "marks": 2,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Why are smoke detectors mounted on the ceiling rather than on the wall or floor?",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "Smoke, fumes, and hot combustion gases from a fire expand and become much less dense than surrounding ambient air. Buoyant convection currents carry them directly upward to accumulate beneath the ceiling, triggering the smoke alarm in the earliest stages of a fire.",
