     "type": "short_answer",
     "marks": 3,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Explain why we prefer to wear white or light-coloured clothes in summer and dark-coloured clothes in winter.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "Thermal radiation does not require a medium and is absorbed or reflected depending on surface coloration:Summer: Light-coloured and white surfaces reflect most of the incident solar radiant heat and absorb very little, keeping our bodies cool and comfortable.Winter: Dark-coloured and black surfaces absorb the maximum amount of radiant heat from the sun and ambient surroundings, helping maintain cozy body warmth.",
