     "marks": 2,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "How does heat from the Sun reach the Earth across interplanetary space?",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "Between the Sun and Earth's atmosphere lies a vast vacuum spanning approximately 150 million kilometres. Neither conduction nor convection can operate without a material medium. Heat travels across this void as thermal radiation (electromagnetic infrared waves) propagating at the speed of light ($3 \\times 10^8\\text{ m/s}$).",
