     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Explain Galileo's discovery regarding the simple pendulum at Pisa Cathedral.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "In 1583, Galileo Galilei observed a swinging chandelier in Pisa Cathedral and timed the oscillations against his own pulse. He discovered that a pendulum of a given length always takes the exact same time to complete one swing, regardless of amplitude. This property is known as isochronism and laid the foundation for pendulum clocks.",
