     "marks": 2,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "How does a distance-time graph show that a body is at rest?",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "When a body is at rest (stationary), its distance from the origin does not change as time elapses. Hence, the graph is a horizontal straight line parallel to the time axis (Slope = 0).",
