     "type": "short_answer",
     "marks": 2,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Interpret the physical meaning of the slope of a Distance-Time graph.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "The slope (gradient) of a Distance-Time graph is given by: $$\\text{Slope} = \\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = \\frac{\\text{Change in Distance}}{\\text{Change in Time}} = \\text{Speed}$$. A steeper slope represents higher speed.",
     "explanation": "Official textbook model solution and marking rubric breakdown."
