     "subject": "science",
     "chapter_num": "13",
     "chapter_title": "Understanding Gender",
     "type": "long_answer",
     "marks": 5,
     "difficulty": "medium",
     "question": "Explain the key features, historical or geographical significance, and characteristics of 13.5 & 13.6 Social Reformers & Government Initiatives Fighting for Rights.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "• Raja Rammohan Roy: Led movement to abolish Sati in 1829. • Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar: Fought for the Hindu Widow Remarriage Act (1856). • Savitribai & Jyotirao Phule: Started the first Indian school for girls in Pune (1848). • Pandita Ramabai: Founded Sarada Sadan in Mumbai for widows. • Begum Rokeya Sakhawat Hossain: Championed Muslim girls' education.",
     "explanation": "Core curriculum conceptual foundation for 13.5 & 13.6 Social Reformers & Government Initiatives Fighting for Rights."
