     "question": "Differentiate between the three types of earthquake waves.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "1. **P-Waves (Primary / Longitudinal waves)**: Fastest waves that travel through solids, liquids, and gases via compressional push-pull action. 2. **S-Waves (Secondary / Transverse waves)**: Slower waves that travel only through solids, moving particles perpendicular to wave direction. 3. **L-Waves (Surface waves)**: Travel along Earth's surface and cause the greatest ground displacement and structural damage.",
