     "question": "Describe the administrative system of the Mauryan Empire, highlighting the roles of the capital and provincial governors.",
     "options": [],
     "answer": "The Mauryan Empire established a vast, highly organized administrative apparatus: • **Central Administration (Pataliputra)**: Directly controlled by the Emperor with advice from the Council of Ministers (*Mantriparishad*). Revenue officials (*Samaharta*) collected taxes, and royal spies kept the Emperor informed of administrative conduct. • **Provincial Administration**: Divided into provinces governed from key urban hubs like Taxila (north-west trade corridor) and Ujjain (route from north to south). Royal princes (*Kumaras*) served as provincial governors. • **Tribute Collection in Forest Regions**: Forest dwellers provided tribute in elephants, timber, honey, and wax rather than regular cash taxes.",
