     "answer": "In the adjoining figure of intersecting lines forming angles 1, 2, 3, 4, name: (a) Vertically opposite angles (b) Linear pairs View Solution (a) Vertically opposite angles: $\\mathbf{\u0007ngle 1 ext{ and } \u0007ngle 3}$, and $\\mathbf{\u0007ngle 2 ext{ and } \u0007ngle 4}$. (b) Linear pairs: $\\mathbf{(\u0007ngle 1, \u0007ngle 2), (\u0007ngle 2, \u0007ngle 3), (\u0007ngle 3, \u0007ngle 4), (\u0007ngle 4, \u0007ngle 1)}$.",
