     "answer": "(a) In $ riangle XYZ$, identify the median and altitude. (b) In $ riangle ABC$, identify the median and altitude. Core Question: In which cases do the medians and altitudes overlap? View Solution & Geometrical Rules Definitions: • Median: Line segment connecting a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side. • Altitude: Perpendicular line segment dropped from a vertex to the line containing the opposite side. When do they overlap (coincide)? 1. In an Equilateral Triangle , all three medians coincide with their respective altitudes. 2. In an Isosceles Triangle , the median and altitude drawn from the vertex angle between the two equal sides to the base overlap exactly!",
