     "options": [],
     "answer": "Look at the figure shown alongside and fill in the blanks: (a) $\u0007ngle ACR = ext{______} + ext{______}$ (b) $\u0007ngle PAB = ext{______} + ext{______}$ (c) $\u0007ngle QBC = ext{______} + ext{______}$ View Solution Exterior Angle Property: An exterior angle of a triangle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles. (a) $\u0007ngle ACR = \\mathbf{\u0007ngle A + \u0007ngle B}$ (or $\u0007ngle CAB + \u0007ngle CBA$) (b) $\u0007ngle PAB = \\mathbf{\u0007ngle B + \u0007ngle C}$ (or $\u0007ngle ABC + \u0007ngle ACB$) (c) $\u0007ngle QBC = \\mathbf{\u0007ngle A + \u0007ngle C}$ (or $\u0007ngle BAC + \u0007ngle BCA$)",
